CORE gcc-only
main.i
--arch x86_64 --unwind 5 --unwinding-assertions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
approximating inline assembly
--
The outer loop is fully unwound (five iterations cover the four lock/unlock
pairs), so a failing unwinding assertion could only come from a spin loop that
symbolic execution cannot resolve because the lock word is not a constant.
